e)(f\"{self.name}: {e}\"). For ValueError fine.\n\nlogger.py: extend NewLineFormatter with keyword-only max_message_chars. Validation: must be int >=32, bool not int.\n\nformat: after super().format(record) computing msg... but we need to truncate the message body, not the whole formatted string. Approach: in format, compute the record \"message\" first: super().format calls record.getMessage() and sets record.message. Then we could truncate. But truncating after formatting would require locating message within msg and handling exc_info/stack_info appended.\n\nBetter approach: before calling super().format, build a shallow copy of the record? Requirement 5: \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\" — can't modify shared original record. So we must not set record.msg. Instead compute the truncated message ourselves and format manually.\n\nOptions: create a copy.copy(record) and set its msg/args to truncated, keeping exc_info/stack_info? But requirement says the record later given to full handler must retain full message — using copy is fine as we don't mutate the original.\n\nBut colors, multi-line prefix use record.message from super().format. Using a copy: `record = copy.copy(record)` — copy.copy on LogRecord is supported (copy module allows). Then set msg = truncated, args = None? Careful: if we set record.message already... Formatter.format does: record.message = record.getMessage(); then uses format string. So if we set copy.msg = truncated_str and copy.args = None, getMessage returns truncated string. But if keep_full_message is exactly True, don't truncate.\n\nAlso requirement: \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度\" — compute message via record.getMessage(), then truncate.\n\nImplementation without copy module alternative: use `log_record = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)`? Simpler: import copy.\n\nCareful about exc_info: copy.copy keeps exc_info, stack_info attributes; format() will still append traceback. Good. But the copy's `message` attribute may exist already from previous handler (since same record processed by other handler first, record.message set). copy.copy copies it; format() overwrites with new getMessage anyway.\n\nHmm but if we truncate: prefix computation uses `msg[: msg.find(record.message)]`; record is now the copy with truncated message and record.message = truncated. Fine.\n\nAlso for color and everything unchanged.\n\nAlternatively avoid copy entirely: build the truncation into a \"record_copy\". Let's use copy.\n\nLet's write:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars: int | None = None) -> None:\n    super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n    self.high_precision = high_precision\n    self.use_color = use_color\n    if max_message_chars is not None:\n        if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n            raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS} or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n        if max_message_chars < _MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS:\n            raise ValueError(...)\n    self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nTruncation helper:\n\n```python\n_OMITTED_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS = 32\n\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, max_chars: int) -> str:\n    if len(message) <= max_chars:\n        return message\n    marker = _OMITTED_MARKER\n    remaining = max_chars - len(marker)\n    if remaining <= 0:\n        return marker[:max_chars]\n    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail = remaining - head\n    return f\"{message[:head]}{marker}{message[len(message) - tail:] if tail else ''}\"\n```\n\nCheck example: budget 32, marker 15, remaining 17, head = 9, tail = 8. ✓\n\nformat:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n    if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        truncated = _truncate_message(message, max